            <ArticleTitle>An unusual case of Churg-Strauss syndrome and a shrinking renal mass.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>183-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Churg-Strauss syndrome is a multisystem disorder characterized by allergic rhinitis, asthma and eosinophilia [Churg and Strauss 1951, Noth et al. 2003]. We report a case of Churg-Strauss syndrome associated with a complex renal mass, which resolved with immunosuppressive therapy.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
